! mcp_bootstrap_p119.strap -- the tail of the PRIME routine and the
! start of the dispatcher's error-exit block, printed page 119.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.126, header read and not assumed:
! the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11011MCP
! CARD ID EA000100   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 119".
!
! Fifty lines, serials EA000100 (line 1) .. EA000147 (line 50) --
! the same EA deck the pages before this one are punching, not a new
! one.  Forty-nine lines carry a LOCATION; line 47 is a CNOP that
! emits nothing (see below).  215572.00 .. 215634.00.
!
! FORTY-EIGHT SERIALS FOR FIFTY LINES, and the two repeats are not
! misreads -- at 1200 dpi lines 42 and 43 both print EA000141 and
! lines 45 and 46 both print EA000143.  Each repeat is a SIC paired
! with the branch that must follow it ("SIC,S DISIC" then
! "B,S DISP"), i.e. two statements punched on one card.  That is
! STRAP's own rule showing in the card column: strap_asm refuses a
! SIC that is not immediately followed by a half-word branch.
! printed p.118 does the same thing once, at its lines 26 and 27.
!
! CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED: printed p.118's serial column was rendered
! for this (PDF p.125, x=5700 at 400 dpi).  It runs EA000050 ..
! EA000098 over fifty lines, with its own repeat at EA000075.  So
! this IS the same EA deck -- and EA000099 is printed on neither
! page.  A one-serial gap across the page break, recorded and not
! explained.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  Lines 1-40 are the tail of the PRIME routine:
! p.103 line 41 puts SPRIME at 215570.00, two words before line 1,
! and the names (MPR2, MPR4A/4B, MPR5A, MPR6A/6B, MPR7, MPR8) and
! comments ("-PRIME Q EMPTY", "-PRIME Q FULL", "-PARAM IN PRIME Q.")
! agree.  Lines 41-50 begin the error-exit block that printed p.120
! continues: each entry is LVI,$14,<error code>; SIC,SDISIC; B,SDISP,
! which is exactly the sequence the MCP System Analysis Guide
! describes ("SDISP Error; code in $14 ... Type 1 (MNOMCP) illegal IF
! interrupt").
!
! >>> THE ORIGIN IS NOT SET ON THIS PAGE. <<<  There is no SLC row
! here; printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." is still the last
! one transcribed, and printed pp.113-118 are not transcribed yet.
! The SLC below is therefore written from THIS page's own first
! LOCATION -- but the join to the page before IS checked, not
! assumed.  printed p.118's bottom rows were rendered (PDF p.125):
!
!   line 48  215570.00  000020.00 80  215622.12 A0  S PRIME TI,5,$0,MPR8
!   line 49  215571.00  000000.03 01                S PRIMR LVI,$1,0
!   line 50  215571.40  000000.04 01                LV,$2,0.0($1)
!
! Line 50 is a half word, so the counter leaves printed p.118 at
! 215572.00, which is this page's line 1.  CONTIGUOUS.  Three more
! things fall out of those three rows, all of them independent
! confirmations of values this deck carries:
!   * S PRIME is at 215570.00, exactly where printed p.103 line 41
!     SYNs it -- so this page really is the PRIME routine's body,
!     entered two words above line 1;
!   * p.118 line 48's "TI,5,$0,MPR8" prints 215622.12, which is
!     MPR8 at 215622.00 read off a DIFFERENT page;
!   * S PRIMR is at 215571.00, where printed p.103 SYNs it too.
!
! TAIL SCOPE: pp.99+ are outside the TAIL,(2)G block printed p.2
! opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with UNTAIL,(2), so a name
! here may legitimately repeat a pp.2-98 name at another address.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS SETTLED, AND HOW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) MNOMCP (line 41).  The page prints "M NC MCP".  The typeset
!     manual decides it: docs/ocr/C22-6728_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_
!     Guide.txt and its -1 revision both print "Type 1 (MNOMCP)
!     illegal IF interrupt" -- MNOMCP 2, NCMCP 0 over all of
!     docs/ocr/ -- and this row's own comment is
!     "- ILLEGAL IF INTERRUPT".  printed p.117 line 12 branches here
!     ("BZXE,M NC MCP") and is the only other instance in the
!     listing, printed with the same damaged O.
!
! (2) MOPCI (line 44).  The page prints "M CP CI" in the NAME column
!     and "S CP C I" in the statement, but the comment is
!     "- ILLEGAL OP CODE" and docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt prints
!     the reference as English three times: "BZRZ,M OP CI" and
!     "BZXL,M OP CI" on printed p.117 (lines 15 and 26) and
!     "B,M OP CI  -INVALID OP" on printed p.178.  OP, not CP.
!
!     >>> AND THAT MAKES decks/mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap WRONG. <<<
!     p.107 line 5 defines this symbol and the deck spells it SCPCI;
!     its own transcribed comment is "- 2 PSEUDO CP CODE INVALID",
!     which is PSEUDO OP CODE INVALID.  The symbol is SOPCI at
!     010002.00.  This deck writes SOPCI.  A merged image built from
!     p.107 and this page would fail on an undefined symbol until
!     p.107 is corrected -- that is the right failure to have.
!
! (3) MIFTTT, MIFAS, MPRMQK are spelled by the typeset manual too
!     (one/two hits each in C22-6728, zero for any variant).
!
! (4) B's op byte is 00, not C0.  Lines 31, 34, 38, 43 and 46 print
!     a round glyph that reads C at 900 dpi; printed p.112's landed
!     rows print B as "216333.10 00" fourteen times, and the octal
!     field two characters earlier on these same rows drops ink the
!     same way.  Observed C may be a damaged 0; observed 0 is never
!     a damaged C.
!
! (5) D0 on lines 11, 20 and 24 IS a D: at 1500 dpi the glyph has the
!     straight vertical left stem and squared corners that the round
!     0/C of the octal field in the same row does not.
!
! (6) The LOCATION column carries a trailing asterisk on lines 6, 25,
!     40 and 48.  That is the unexplained marker of
!     docs/listing_typography.md 12 (printed p.3's note); it changes
!     no assembled bit.  Every LINE NUMBER also carries one, as on
!     pp.99-112.  A stray ink dot sits in the NAME column between
!     lines 24 and 25 and is not a character.
!
! (7) Line 40 really is "DRZ(BU,0),(5)", one glyph, against line 48's
!     two-glyph "DRZ(BU,64),(1)" in the same column -- compared side
!     by side at 1800 dpi.  It reserves five words all the same
!     (215622.00 -> 215627.00, printed 000005.00), and that is
!     STRAP's documented rule, not an inference from the assembler:
!     C28-6129 STRAP-II (PDF p.11) says "If the field length is
!     null, a field length of zero (effectively 64 -- see 7030
!     Reference Manual -- except in the case of VFL immediate where
!     it is 24) is compiled."  A written 0 and a null field compile
!     the same zero, and zero means 64.
!
! (8) Line 47 prints NO location and NO binary: line 46 is a half
!     word that leaves the counter at 215632.00, already full-word
!     aligned, so its CNOP emits nothing.  Line 39's CNOP does emit
!     (000000.30 00), because line 38 left the counter at .40.  No
!     !CHECK for line 47.
!
! (9) Line 33's comment really ends "REGSZ" at 1500 dpi.  Transcribed
!     as printed.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---- externals, with where each value was read ---------------------
MIFTTT  SYN, (8)215666.0             ! line 2 prints 215566.04 for
                                      !   MIFTTT-64.0($2); 64.0 is a
                                      !   bare decimal literal = 0o100
                                      !   words.  printed p.121 heads
                                      !   "IF ANALYZER TABLE OF
                                      !   TENTACLE ADDRESSES" and its
                                      !   line 22 carries 215666.00.
MPRMQK  SYN, (8)215640.0             ! p.120 line  6 "M PRM QK DRZ"
MPRMER  SYN, (8)215641.0             ! p.120 line  7 "M PRM ER LVI,"
MC1     SYN, (8)215637.0             ! p.120 line  4 "M C 1 DD(BU,24)"
MPQR    SYN, (8)215643.0             ! p.120 line 10 defines it at
                                      !   215643.00.  SPELLING IS
                                      !   SINGLE-SOURCE: only line 35
                                      !   here prints the letters, and
                                      !   p.120's OCR garbles the Q to
                                      !   "MP @ RR".  No MPQR anywhere
                                      !   in docs/ocr/ (the MPOR hits
                                      !   are all inside TEMPORARY).
MR4     SYN, (8)215644.0             ! p.120 line 11 "M R 4 DRZ"
MR5     SYN, (8)215645.0             ! p.120 line 12 "M R 5 DRZ"
SIFERR  SYN, (8)010001.0             ! p.107 line  4
SOPCI   SYN, (8)010002.0             ! p.107 line  5 (spelled SCPCI
                                      !   there -- see note (2))
SIFAS   SYN, (8)004012.0             ! p.107 line 34
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40            ! p.103; lines 42/45 print it
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0             ! lines 43/46 print 217372.10 and
                                      !   B prints its target + .10
                                      !   (line 31: MPR4B 215606.40 ->
                                      !   215606.50)

        SLC, (8)215572.00

! ---- the PRIME routine, continued ----------------------------------
        CM0000(BU,1), $2+.24         ! line  1
        LV, 2, MIFTTT-64.0($2)       ! line  2 -GET ADDRESS OF TT
        L(BU,4), 0.0($2), -19        ! line  3 -N IN ACC
        LV, $0, $L                   ! line  4
        V+, $0, $0                   ! line  5 -19 BIT VALUE =18 BIT
                                      !           COUNT
        LC, $4, $0                   ! line  6
        LV, $0, MPRMQK               ! line  7
MPR2    BXVZZ, MPR7                  ! line  8 -PRIME Q EMPTY
        LV, $3, $1                   ! line  9
        V+, $3, $L                   ! line 10
        SVA, 3, MPR6B                ! line 11 -SET RETURN ADDRESS
        V+, 0, $L                    ! line 12
        KVI, $0, 15.0                ! line 13
        BXHZ, MPRMER                 ! line 14 -PRIME Q FULL
        SV, $0, MPRMQK               ! line 15 - NEW Q COUNT
        LX, $3, MR4                  ! line 16
        LI(BU,24), .9, -24           ! line 17
        V+, $2, $L                   ! line 18 -FORM EFF. BIT
MPR4A   L(V+I)(BU,32), .32($1)       ! line 19
        ST(V+ICR)(BU,32), .32($3)    ! line 20 -PARAM IN PRIME Q.
MPR4B   CBZ, $4, MPR6A               ! line 21
        V+, $2, MC1                  ! line 22 -ADD. 2 FOR NEXT FORM
                                      !           EFF
        BZB, 0.0($2), MPR4A          ! line 23 -NO FORM EFF
        SVA, $1, MPR5A               ! line 24
        V+I, 1, .32                  ! line 25
        SWAPI, 4, $1, MPR8+1.0       ! line 26
MPR5A   LVE, $0, $                   ! line 27 -FORM EFF
        SWAPI, 4, $1, MPR8+1.0       ! line 28
        SV, 0, 0($3)                 ! line 29
        V+ICR, 3, .32                ! line 30
        B, MPR4B                     ! line 31
MPR6A   SX, 3, MR4                   ! line 32 -SAVE PRIME CONTROL
        TI, 5, MPR8, $0              ! line 33 -RESTORE USED X REGSZ
MPR6B   B, $                         ! line 34 -RETURN DISABLED
MPR7    LX, $3, MPQR                 ! line 35
        SX, $3, MR4                  ! line 36 -REFILL PRIME CONTROL
        SX, $3, MR5                  ! line 37 -REFILL UNPRIME CONTROL
        B, MPR2+.32                  ! line 38
        CNOP                         ! line 39
MPR8    DRZ(BU,0), (5)               ! line 40

! ---- the error exits -----------------------------------------------
MNOMCP  LVI, $14, SIFERR             ! line 41 - ILLEGAL IF INTERRUPT
        SIC, SDISIC                  ! line 42
        B, SDISP                     ! line 43
MOPCI   LVI, 14, SOPCI               ! line 44 - ILLEGAL OP CODE
        SIC, SDISIC                  ! line 45
        B, SDISP                     ! line 46
        CNOP                         ! line 47 (emits nothing)
        DRZ(BU,64), (1)              ! line 48
MMK1    INDMK, .53, .55(.63)21       ! line 49
MIFAS   LVI, $14, SIFAS              ! line 50

